    "title"             "Knox Relay"
    "description"       "Server-side bridge mod for remote server management. Exports game state, inventory snapshots, player positions, progression and live character vitals, and processes item delivery and money deposit queues via file-based JSON communication. Provides /account register for linking a character to a website account."
    "changenote"        "[h1]1.10 — /account register[/h1]\n[b]Added[/b]\n[list]\n[*]/account register in game. It asks the website to open a registration for the character you are playing, and the website answers within a few seconds with a six-character code. You finish signing up in a browser with that code, an email and a password, and the account is created already carrying the character's name.\n[*]The code is shown to you alone — drawn on your own screen, never sent to a chat channel. Chat is echoed into the server log, where every other log reader would see it.\n[*]Running the command again replaces your outstanding code rather than adding a second, so a character never has two live codes.\n[/list]\n[b]Notes[/b]\nAccounts can only be made this way, which is the point: there is no sign-up form that works without a character, so no account can exist that is not attached to somebody who actually plays here. If the website does not answer within about thirty seconds the mod says so and asks you to try again, rather than leaving you watching nothing happen. Servers on 1.9 or earlier have no such command and therefore no way to make an account."
}
